 when students can interact, experiment, make mistakes, observe outcomes and apply concepts."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base leading-8 text-muted-foreground sm:text-lg","children":"Science Lab follows a Learning by Doing approach, helping students move from understanding a concept to exploring its practical application. Interactive simulations create an environment where learners can experiment repeatedly and develop a deeper understanding of scientific principles."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-foreground sm:text-2xl","children":"Learn → Experiment → Observe → Understand → Apply"}]]}]]}],["$","$L17",null,{"delay":0.08,"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card shadow-sm","children":["$","$Lb",null,{"src":"/images/science-lab-virtual-experiment.jpg","alt":"Student exploring an interactive virtual science experiment","width":700,"height":392,"sizes":"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 420px","className":"aspect-[16/9] w-full object-cover"}]}]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"id":"science-lab-learning-banners","className":"border-y border-border bg-[#e8f4f8] py-16 sm:py-24","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container-site","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2","children":[["$","$L17","Learning by Doing",{"delay":0,"children":["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-[#0F4C81]/15 bg-white p-3 shadow-[0_12px_36px_rgba(15,76,129,0.1)]","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex aspect-[4/3] items-center justify-center overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-white","children":["$","$Lb",null,{"src":"/images/science-lab-learning-by-doing.png","alt":"Learning by Doing science learning graphic","width":493,"height":370,"sizes":"(min-width: 1024px) 50vw, 100vw","className":"h-full w-full object-contain"}]}],"$L18"]}]}],"$L19"]}]}]}],"$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23"]
